---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-400.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-500.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-600.css";
import "@fontsource/inter/latin-700.css";
import "@fontsource/plus-jakarta-sans/latin-600.css";
import "@fontsource/plus-jakarta-sans/latin-700.css";
import "@fontsource/plus-jakarta-sans/latin-800.css";
import "../styles/site.css";

const installCmd = `npx shadcn add https://uiforagents.com/registries/ocean-calm/ocean-calm.json`;
const installConfig = JSON.stringify(
  {
    registries: {
      "@uiforagents": "https://uiforagents.com/registries/{name}/{name}.json",
    },
  },
  null,
  2
);
---
<Base title="Launch: the identity catalogue is live - uiforagents" description="uiforagents pivots from a vanilla UI kit to a catalogue of design identities for agent-built apps: five identities across two lanes, one install command, and an agent prompt-pack.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 24px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Launch - October 2026</p>
      <h1>The identity catalogue is live</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        uiforagents is now a catalogue of design identities for agent-built apps: complete,
        opinionated systems your agent follows. Pick an identity, hand your agent the prompt-pack,
        and ship. Five ship today: the shadcn identities
        <a href="/identities/ocean-calm/">ocean-calm</a>, <a href="/identities/nairobi-noon/">nairobi-noon</a>,
        and <a href="/identities/graphite-terminal/">graphite-terminal</a>, plus the pure-CSS
        artifact identities <a href="/identities/reading-room/">reading-room</a> and
        <a href="/identities/midnight-bulletin/">midnight-bulletin</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
      <div class="about-copy">
        <h2>The pivot</h2>
        <p>
          uiforagents started as an agent-first vanilla UI kit: copy-in HTML/CSS/JS components with
          zero runtime dependencies. It proved the idea that agents ship production UI when the
          design decisions are made for them - but it also proved that components are the wrong
          unit. A pile of well-styled parts still leaves every product decision open: which font,
          how dense, what radius, when to move. Agents don't need more parts; they need a point of
          view.
        </p>
        <p>
          So the kit became a catalogue of <strong>design identities</strong>. Each identity bundles
          theme tokens, component overrides, composed blocks, fonts, motion defaults, and an agent
          prompt-pack into one installable payload. The identity is the contract: no design
          deliberation, no drift between pages. The vanilla kit was retired in October 2026; the full
          story and the what-changed note live on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>How to use an identity with your agent</h2>
        <p>
          Install it into any shadcn/ui + Tailwind v4 app (React 18+) by URL - swap the slug for any
          identity in the catalogue:
        </p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>{installCmd}</code></pre>
        <p>
          Or register the <code>@uiforagents</code> namespace once in <code>components.json</code>,
          then install by name:
        </p>
        <pre class="code-block"><code>{installConfig}</code></pre>
        <p class="code-note">Then: <code>npx shadcn add @uiforagents/ocean-calm</code> (any slug works in place of <code>ocean-calm</code>).</p>
        <p>
          Next, attach the identity's <a href="/prompt-packs/ocean-calm.md">prompt-pack.md</a> to
          every agent building UI. The pack encodes the identity's design decisions - typography,
          color rules, density, component choices, do/don'ts - so the agent stops improvising design
          and starts shipping. Humans pick the identity; the agent builds with it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Want to see an identity first? Every identity page renders its full suite inline - the
          real blocks wearing the identity, right on the page. Start at
          <a href="/identities/graphite-terminal/">graphite-terminal</a> or browse the
          <a href="/#identities">gallery</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Not every build is a shadcn app. The catalogue also carries <strong>pure-CSS artifact
          identities</strong> for self-contained HTML artifacts - no install, no JavaScript, no
          framework. Copy the identity's <code>foundation.css</code> into the page, attach the
          prompt-pack, and ship; the <a href="/identities/reading-room/">reading-room</a> page shows
          the pattern with its live demo.
        </p>

        <h2>What's next</h2>
        <p>
          More identities across new moods and surfaces, continuing the queued-card pattern on the
          landing gallery, and tighter agent integration as the registry ecosystem grows. The
          catalogue, licenses, and roadmap are on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
